{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AWK4FXVntUiypdCUVrdJ7Q","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd033-sha512sum\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/sha512sum: Compute and Check SHA-512 Message Digests\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships shasum -a 512 rather than sha512sum; the invocation differs from GNU\n6\t  sha512sum. Scripts that generate or verify SHA-512 checksums using the GNU format\n7\t  must use the Homebrew reference binary. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew\n8\t  GNU reference binary (gsha512sum, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag\n9\t  combinations, using crypto/sha512 from the Go standard library, verified by\n10\t  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n11\t\n12\tgoals:\n13\t  - G1: Compute SHA-512 digests for one or more files or stdin and print them in GNU format, matching gsha512sum behavior.\n14\t  - G2: Support --check (-c) to verify a checksum file and report mismatches.\n15\t  - G3: Support --binary (-b), --text (-t), and --tag output format flags.\n16\t\n17\trequirements:\n18\t  R1:\n19\t    title: Digest computation\n20\t    items:\n21\t      - R1.1:\n22\t          text: Must compute the SHA-512 digest of each named file and write one line per file in the format \"HASH  FILENAME\" (text mode) or \"HASH *FILENAME\" (binary mode). The default is text mode.\n23\t      - R1.2:\n24\t          text: Must read from stdin and print \"HASH  -\" when no file arguments are given or when \"-\" is provided as a filename.\n25\t      - R1.3:\n26\t          text: --tag must use BSD-style output format \"SHA512 (FILENAME) = HASH\".\n27\t      - R1.4:\n28\t          text: Must exit 1 when any named file cannot be opened, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n29\t\n30\t  R2:\n31\t    title: Checksum verification (--check, -c)\n32\t    items:\n33\t      - R2.1:\n34\t          text: \"--check FILE must read FILE, parse each line (GNU or BSD tag format), recompute the SHA-512 digest, and compare to the stored hash.\"\n35\t      - R2.2:\n36\t          text: 'Must print \"FILENAME: OK\" or \"FILENAME: FAILED\" for each entry. Must exit 1 if any check fails.'\n37\t      - R2.3:\n38\t          text: --warn prints a warning for each malformed line. --quiet suppresses OK lines. --status suppresses all output.\n39\t\n40\t  R3:\n41\t    title: Binary and text mode flags\n42\t    items:\n43\t      - R3.1:\n44\t          text: -b marks input as binary; output uses \"HASH *FILENAME\". -t (default) uses \"HASH  FILENAME\".\n45\t      - R3.2:\n46\t          text: --tag produces BSD tag format regardless of -b/-t.\n47\t\n48\t  R4:\n49\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n50\t    items:\n51\t      - R4.1:\n52\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed and all verified digests match.\n53\t      - R4.2:\n54\t          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened, any digest fails, or the checksum file is unreadable.\n55\t      - R4.3:\n56\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n57\t\n58\tnon_goals:\n59\t  - cmd/sha512sum does not implement HMAC-SHA512 or keyed variants.\n60\t  - cmd/sha512sum does not implement SHA-384 or SHA-512/256 truncations.\n61\t\n62\tpackage_contract:\n63\t  imports:\n64\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/hashutil\n65\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n66\t\n67\tacceptance_criteria:\n68\t  - id: AC1\n69\t    criterion: \"sha512sum on a known file produces the correct SHA-512 hash in GNU format, matching gsha512sum.\"\n70\t    traces:\n71\t      - R1.1\n72\t      - R1.2\n73\t      - R1.3\n74\t      - R1.4\n75\t  - id: AC2\n76\t    criterion: \"sha512sum --check on a valid checksum file exits 0 and prints 'FILENAME: OK' for each entry.\"\n77\t    traces:\n78\t      - R1.4\n79\t      - R2.1\n80\t      - R2.2\n81\t      - R4.1\n82\t      - R4.2\n83\t      - R4.3\n84\t  - id: AC3\n85\t    criterion: \"sha512sum --check on a file with a mismatch exits 1 and prints 'FILENAME: FAILED'.\"\n86\t    traces:\n87\t      - R1.4\n88\t      - R2.1\n89\t      - R2.2\n90\t      - R4.1\n91\t      - R4.2\n92\t      - R4.3\n93\t  - id: AC4\n94\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gsha512sum passes for all required test cases.\"\n95\t    traces:\n96\t      - R1.1\n97\t      - R1.2\n98\t      - R1.3\n99\t      - R1.4\n100\t  - id: AC5\n101\t    criterion: \"cmd/sha512sum compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n102\t    traces:\n103\t      - R1.1\n104\t      - R1.2\n105\t      - R1.3\n106\t      - R1.4\n107\t      - R2.1\n108\t      - R2.2\n109\t      - R2.3\n110\t      - R3.1\n111\t      - R3.2\n112\t      - R4.1\n113\t      - R4.2\n114\t      - R4.3\n115\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c641083-6591-4356-83cb-b05211379ef1","uuid":"26fe1313-f635-4252-ac4d-bfe1d552c4e8","timestamp":"2026-05-20T00:00:00.358Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5322/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd033-sha512sum.yaml","content":"id: srd033-sha512sum\ntitle: \"cmd/sha512sum: Compute and Check SHA-512 Message Digests\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships shasum -a 512 rather than sha512sum; the invocation differs from GNU\n  sha512sum. Scripts that generate or verify SHA-512 checksums using the GNU format\n  must use the Homebrew reference binary. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew\n  GNU reference binary (gsha512sum, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag\n  combinations, using crypto/sha512 from the Go standard library, verified by\n  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Compute SHA-512 digests for one or more files or stdin and print them in GNU format, matching gsha512sum behavior.\n  - G2: Support --check (-c) to verify a checksum file and report mismatches.\n  - G3: Support --binary (-b), --text (-t), and --tag output format flags.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Digest computation\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must compute the SHA-512 digest of each named file and write one line per file in the format \"HASH  FILENAME\" (text mode) or \"HASH *FILENAME\" (binary mode). The default is text mode.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must read from stdin and print \"HASH  -\" when no file arguments are given or when \"-\" is provided as a filename.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: --tag must use BSD-style output format \"SHA512 (FILENAME) = HASH\".\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any named file cannot be opened, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Checksum verification (--check, -c)\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"--check FILE must read FILE, parse each line (GNU or BSD tag format), recompute the SHA-512 digest, and compare to the stored hash.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: 'Must print \"FILENAME: OK\" or \"FILENAME: FAILED\" for each entry. Must exit 1 if any check fails.'\n      - R2.3:\n          text: --warn prints a warning for each malformed line. --quiet suppresses OK lines. --status suppresses all output.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Binary and text mode flags\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: -b marks input as binary; output uses \"HASH *FILENAME\". -t (default) uses \"HASH  FILENAME\".\n      - R3.2:\n          text: --tag produces BSD tag format regardless of -b/-t.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed and all verified digests match.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened, any digest fails, or the checksum file is unreadable.\n      - R4.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/sha512sum does not implement HMAC-SHA512 or keyed variants.\n  - cmd/sha512sum does not implement SHA-384 or SHA-512/256 truncations.\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/hashutil\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"sha512sum on a known file produces the correct SHA-512 hash in GNU format, matching gsha512sum.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"sha512sum --check on a valid checksum file exits 0 and prints 'FILENAME: OK' for each entry.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"sha512sum --check on a file with a mismatch exits 1 and prints 'FILENAME: FAILED'.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gsha512sum passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/sha512sum compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n","numLines":115,"startLine":1,"totalLines":115}}}
