{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user submitted a stitch task (Task ID 5322) titled \"[stitch] cmd/sha512sum completion (srd033 R3.2, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3)\". The task requires implementing four specific requirements for the sha512sum utility:\n   - **R1**: Add `--strict` flag that treats improperly formatted checksum lines as errors during `--check` mode, causing non-zero exit\n   - **R2**: Ensure exit code 0 on success, exit code 1 on any verification failure or operational error\n   - **R3**: Print diagnostic messages to stderr for missing/unreadable files in GNU format (`sha512sum: FILENAME: REASON`), continuing to process remaining files\n   - **R4**: Support `--version` and `--help` flags with GNU-standard output format\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/sha512sum/main.go` and `cmd/sha512sum/sha512sum_test.go` only.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU sha512sum, verified via differential testing against `gsha512sum` (Homebrew)\n   - `pkg/hashutil` shared library provides `HashConfig`, `CheckOptions`, `VerifyChecksums`, `DigestFiles`, `ParseChecksumLine`, `ComputeDigest`, `FormatGNU`, `FormatBSDTag`\n   - `pkg/testutils` provides `DiffTest`, `RunDiffTests`, `BuildBinary`, `NormalizeFunc` for differential testing\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` must be called at start of main\n   - SPDX copyright header required on all Go files\n   - No git commands allowed (orchestrator manages git)\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max\n   - File size limit: 500 lines max\n   - Write all files before building/testing\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd033-sha512sum.yaml**\n     - The SRD for sha512sum. Note: The SRD's R3.2 says \"--tag produces BSD tag format\" and R4.3 says \"Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully\" - but the TASK description maps these IDs to different behaviors (--strict flag and --version/--help). Follow the TASK description's requirement text, not the SRD's literal R3.2/R4.3.\n     - Non-goals: No HMAC-SHA512, no SHA-384/SHA-512/256 truncations.\n\n   - **cmd/sha512sum/main.go** (existing, 172 lines)\n     - Already has: `helpText` const (lines 18-35), `versionText` const (lines 37-38), `parseArgs`, `parseLongFlag`, `parseShortFlags`, `options` struct, `nulWriter`, SIGPIPE handler\n     - Already handles `--help` and `--version` (lines 126-131 in parseLongFlag, calling `os.Exit(0)`)\n     - Already handles `--check` mode with `hashutil.VerifyChecksums` and exit code logic\n     - Already handles `hashutil.DigestFiles` for hashing mode\n     - **Missing**: `--strict` flag in options struct and parsing, strict behavior in check mode\n     - `options` struct has: `binary`, `tag`, `check`, `warn`, `quiet`, `status`, `zero` - needs `strict` added\n     - Error messages for digest mode come from `hashutil.DigestFiles` which formats as `\"file: error\"` - may need to be adjusted to `\"sha512sum: file: error\"` format\n\n   - **cmd/sha512sum/sha512sum_test.go** (existing, 317 lines)\n     - Has `TestDiff` with 33 test cases covering R1.1-R4.2\n     - Has `TestSIGPIPE` for SIGPIPE handling\n     - Has helpers: `sha512hex`, `writeFile`\n     - Uses `discardStderr` normalizer for tests comparing stderr\n     - Creates temp files: hello.txt, empty.txt, various checksum files (valid, multi, mismatch, mixed, malformed, bsd)\n     - **Missing**: Tests for `--strict` mode, `--version`, `--help`\n\n   - **pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go** (read-only context, 130 lines)\n     - `VerifyChecksums(checksumFile string, cfg HashConfig, opts CheckOptions, stdout, stderr io.Writer) (bool, error)` \n     - `verifyOneLine` returns `true` for malformed lines (line 62) - this is the key: with `--strict`, malformed lines should cause failure\n     - `CheckOptions` has `Warn`, `Quiet`, `Status` - does NOT have `Strict`\n     - `DigestFiles` returns exit code int, formats errors as `\"file: error\"` (not `\"sha512sum: file: error\"`)\n     - `openInput` handles \"-\" as stdin\n\n   - **pkg/hashutil/hashconfig.go** (read-only context, 55 lines)\n     - Defines `HashConfig`, `CheckOptions`, `FormatGNU`, `FormatBSDTag`, `ComputeDigest`\n     - Package contract is fixed - CheckOptions has only Warn/Quiet/Status\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Implementation has not started.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Key design challenge identified**: The `--strict` flag needs to be implemented, but `hashutil.CheckOptions` doesn't have a `Strict` field, and the task constrains modifications to only `cmd/sha512sum/main.go` and `cmd/sha512sum/sha512sum_test.go`. \n   - **Possible approach**: Implement strict checking in `main.go` by: (a) reading the checksum file line-by-line using `hashutil.ParseChecksumLine` to detect malformed lines, then combining that with `hashutil.VerifyChecksums` results, OR (b) implementing custom verification in main.go that uses `ParseChecksumLine` and `ComputeDigest` directly with strict logic.\n   - **Error format concern**: `hashutil.DigestFiles` formats errors as `\"file: error\"` but GNU format should be `\"sha512sum: file: error\"`. The existing code in main.go doesn't prefix with \"sha512sum:\" for digest errors since DigestFiles handles that internally. May need to reimplement digest error handling in main.go or accept the hashutil format.\n   - **--help/--version already exist** in the current code, so the task may primarily need test coverage for them plus any format adjustments.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - **Message 1**: The massive task description containing the stitch task specification with all project context, SRDs, architecture, constitutions, constraints, requirements, design decisions, acceptance criteria, shared protocols, and package contracts. Key quote: \"Follow these steps in order. Complete each step before moving to the next.\"\n   - **Message 2**: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Instructing me to create a summary instead of continuing implementation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement `--strict` flag in `cmd/sha512sum/main.go` (options struct, parsing, behavior in check mode)\n   - Ensure exit codes match GNU sha512sum (0 success, 1 failure)\n   - Ensure error messages go to stderr in GNU format (`sha512sum: FILENAME: REASON`)\n   - Verify `--version` and `--help` produce correct output\n   - Add differential tests in `cmd/sha512sum/sha512sum_test.go` for: strict mode, error cases, --version, --help\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/sha512sum/...` to verify no warnings\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/sha512sum/... -count=1` to verify all tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all 5 required files (SRD, main.go, test file, hashutil.go, hashconfig.go) and was about to begin the \"Plan approach\" step (step 2 of the task instructions). I had not yet written any code or made any modifications. The next step would have been to plan the implementation approach for --strict (the main new feature), then write both files in one pass, then build and test.\n\n   The critical implementation decisions still to be made:\n   - How to implement `--strict` without modifying `hashutil` (since only cmd/sha512sum files are in the modification list)\n   - Whether to implement a custom check loop in main.go that uses `hashutil.ParseChecksumLine` and `hashutil.ComputeDigest` directly, adding strict logic on top\n   - Whether the error message format from `hashutil.DigestFiles` (`\"file: error\"`) needs to be changed to `\"sha512sum: file: error\"` at the cmd level\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Implement the changes to `cmd/sha512sum/main.go` and `cmd/sha512sum/sha512sum_test.go`. Specifically:\n   \n   For main.go:\n   - Add `strict bool` to the `options` struct\n   - Add `--strict` to `parseLongFlag` \n   - Add `--strict` to `helpText`\n   - Implement strict check mode: when `opts.strict` is true during `--check`, read the checksum file line-by-line, use `hashutil.ParseChecksumLine` to detect malformed lines, and if any are found, set exit code to 1\n   - The approach should likely involve a custom verification wrapper in main.go that calls into hashutil functions but adds strict behavior on top\n   \n   For sha512sum_test.go:\n   - Add test cases for `--strict` with malformed checksum lines (expect exit 1)\n   - Add test cases for `--strict` with valid checksum files (expect exit 0)\n   - Add test for `--version` output\n   - Add test for `--help` output\n   \n   Then run `go vet ./cmd/sha512sum/...` and `go test ./cmd/sha512sum/... -count=1`.\n\n   Direct quote from the task: \"Implement srd033 R3.2 -- support --strict flag to treat improperly formatted checksum lines as errors during --check mode, causing non-zero exit\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5322/5c641083-6591-4356-83cb-b05211379ef1.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c641083-6591-4356-83cb-b05211379ef1","uuid":"78911f35-3a47-4d6e-9061-84eaf39f42d2","timestamp":"2026-05-20T00:01:37.280Z","isSynthetic":true}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011wiiB2fHnj1AYefCojCzuc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me plan the implementation approach and then implement the changes.\n\nBased on the summary, I need to:\n\n1. Add `--strict` flag to `cmd/sha512sum/main.go`\n2. Implement strict checking behavior (malformed lines cause non-zero exit)\n3. Add tests for `--strict`, `--version`, `--help`\n4. Build and test\n\nThe key challenge: `hashutil.CheckOptions` doesn't have a `Strict` field, and I can only modify cmd/sha512sum files. So I need to implement strict checking in main.go.\n\nThe approach: For strict mode, I'll implement a custom verification loop in main.go that:\n\n\n- Reads the checksum file line by line\n- Uses `hashutil.ParseChecksumLine` to detect malformed lines\n- Verifies each file's digest using `hashutil.ComputeDigest`\n- Treats any malformed lines as failures when `--strict` is enabled\n\nLooking at the existing code more carefully, `VerifyChecksums` already handles verification but treats malformed lines as warnings rather than failures. With `--strict`, I need those to become hard failures. I'll implement a custom verify function in main.go that wraps the line-by-line logic to handle this distinction.\n\nThe existing flow in hashutil.go has `VerifyChecksums` open the file and call `verifyLines`, which scans each line and calls `verifyOneLine`. When `ParseChecksumLine` fails, it currently prints a warning and returns success. Since I can't modify hashutil, I'll write a custom verification function in main.go that opens the file, parses each line, and returns failure when it encounters malformed lines in strict mode.\n\nWriting custom verify function... I'm noticing that the existing error formatting in DigestFiles uses \"file: error\" but GNU sha512sum expects \"sha512sum: file: error\". Since I can only modify the cmd/sha512sum files and not the hashutil package, I'll need to either