s. The stdout output and exit codes will still match between our implementation and gsha512sum.\n\nFor the `check-warn-malformed` test with --warn but no --strict, malformed lines trigger warnings but don't cause a non-zero exit, so exit code 0 is correct when valid lines verify OK. And for the `strict-malformed` test, the exit code should be 1 because --strict makes malformed lines cause a non-zero exit, even though there's also a valid line that verifies correctly.\n\nI'm ready to implement this now.\n\nI'll make the necessary edits to the file: adding bufio to the imports, updating the help text to include --strict, adding the strict field to the options struct, modifying the check block to call runCheck, handling the --strict flag in the long flag parser, and adding the new functions at the end.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19638,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19638},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c641083-6591-4356-83cb-b05211379ef1","uuid":"839060fe-a8b2-465f-802f-4ef43c826b78"}
